    "specPath": "specs/051-anonymous-bearer-challenge/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Spec 025 B-6 says an unauthenticated request to a bearer route answers 401 with the discovery challenge, and calls that challenge the entire bootstrap. Spec 038 B-1 wired the CSRF exemption for bearer routes only for a request that carries an Authorization header, so an anonymous POST meets the double-submit check first and is refused 403 csrf with no WWW-Authenticate. MCP clients open with exactly that request (the MCP authorization flow begins with an anonymous POST), so no MCP client can bootstrap against a cell. This spec makes the exemption depend on the absence of an ambient credential rather than the presence of a bearer one: a request on a declared bearer route that carries no session cookie is exempt, with or without an Authorization header.\n",
    "title": "Anonymous bearer challenge: a declared bearer route exempts a request that carries no session cookie from CSRF, so an anonymous unsafe request is answered with the 401 discovery challenge instead of 403 csrf"
  },
